# O Come, All Ye Faithful, arranged by DeepSeek Flash and SZ. A piano and guitar statement over strings, then the whole hall joins; up a key at the end.
title: O Come, All Ye Faithful
composer: John Francis Wade
arranger: DeepSeek Flash & SZ
about: Its Latin name is Adeste Fideles. John Francis Wade, a Catholic music copyist in London, published it in the 1740s, and Frederick Oakeley translated it into English in 1841. It was once called the Portuguese Hymn because it was heard at the Portuguese embassy chapel in London.
year: around 1743
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: G major
style: cinematic
tempo: 92
time: 4/4

@bars 60-63 tempo=92..72

